From acc3ecb7661f5eee86d5daf7546d64dbbdf07d09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:44:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ParaviewExportResults: other fields written with the
 unknowns, in the same files

A program which exports the unknowns with `ParaviewExportResults` and
other fields at the nodes, for instance an L2 projection of the stresses,
writes them in two ParaView collections: each one writes the whole mesh at
each export. For a polycrystal of 600 grains on one node, written at its 20
time steps, the collection of the von Mises stress takes 4.4 GB, most of it
being its mesh.

`ParaviewExportResults::addField` adds a field written with the unknowns,
in the same files: the mesh is written once per export for all the fields.
Each field is given by a function called at each export, before the files
are written, with the time step stage of the exported unknowns (beginning
of the time step for the export at the initial time, end of the time step
otherwise). It returns a grid function defined on the mesh of the export,
which is registered in the collection for this export only, so that the
function may give another one at the next export; a field defined on
another mesh is refused. Without field, the files are the same as before.
The header of the post-processing is installed: a program builds it,
adds its fields, and gives it to the problem. For a polycrystal of 600
grains on one node, 20 time steps (mm-opera-hpc), the displacement and the
von Mises stress take one collection of 7.5 GB (101 files) against two of
6.5 and 4.7 GB (202 files), written in 255 s against about 354 s.

The export at the initial time and the exports at the end of the time
steps now share one function, which receives the exported unknowns and
their stage, instead of swapping the unknowns kept by the post-processing.

ParaviewExportResultsTest: a field added to the export is written in the
same files as the displacement, with one mesh, at the initial time and at
the end of a time step, its function being called once per export with the
stage of the unknowns; a field defined on another mesh is refused.
